{
  "title": [
    "rms~"
  ],
  "description": "detect RMS amplitude",
  "origin": "ELSE",
  "categories": [
    "Analysis"
  ],
  "inlets": [
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "type": "signals",
          "description": "signal(s) to analyze"
        }
      ],
      "repeat": false
    }
  ],
  "outlets": [
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "description": "RMS value, one per input channel"
        }
      ],
      "repeat": false
    }
  ],
  "arguments": [
    {
      "type": "float",
      "description": "analysis window size in samples",
      "default": "1024"
    },
    {
      "type": "float",
      "description": "hop size in samples",
      "default": "half the window size"
    }
  ],
  "flags": [
    {
      "name": "-lin",
      "description": "sets output to linear amplitude (default dBFS)"
    }
  ],
  "methods": [
    {
      "type": "set <float, float>",
      "description": "sets window and hop size in samples"
    },
    {
      "type": "lin <float>",
      "description": "nonzero sets to linear output"
    }
  ],
  "body": "[rms~] is similar to Pd Vanilla's [env~], but it reports the RMS value in dBFS (default) or in linear amplitude."
}